            "review_title": "Review at Quan 94",
            "review_text": "jp384\nBeijing, China102 contributions\n1\nCrab heaven; tastier & friendlier than the other restaurants in the neighborhood!\nJun 2018 • Couples\nDon't be fooled by the other \"94\" restaurant next door -- this one is the REAL deal! Check the photos to make sure you're at the correct one. This was recommended by foodie friend who frequents HCMC, and it didn't disappoint a crab-lover like me, as long as you know what to order -- so here's what to get:\n\nSoft-shell crab. How could you not love soft shell crab?? What more can I say about it? Crispy, soft, fresh, piping-hot, made-to-order, delicious dipped in sweet chili sauce. Eat with your hands. Drooling just typing about it right now.\n\nCrabmeat stir-fried glass noodles. Generous chunks of hand-picked crabmeat; bouncy, translucent vermicelli noodles; that fragrant whiff of stir-fry deliciousness. I could eat it all day long. Honestly, this dish was so much tastier and higher-quality than the same dish we over-paid for at our five-star hotel. I know.\n\nCrabmeat spring rolls. I didn't know one order came with 5 huge spring rolls. The skin is flakier and crispier than your average Chinese-restaurant spring roll and it's absolutely stuffed with crab and veggies. All the food comes with a huge basket of fresh leaves, herbs and veggies, so we used the lettuce and basil to roll each spring roll with, dunk in sauce and stuff ourselves silly. Heaven.\n\nSnails stir-fried in sweet soy sauce. Sweet and salty, with a nice funky brininess that I enjoy. Definitely a great beer snack to get your fingers messy with. \n\nAll food comes with aforementioned generous basket of veggies and herbs, plus delicious pickled carrots, seeet chili sauce, and cold rice noodles -- an awesome addition to the lettuce leaf \"tacos\" you'll be making with all those greens and your soft shell crab or spring rolls:\n\nTip: DON'T feel you need to order a whole crab, which are expensive at $30 USD per crab. We almost did, but found we were perfectly satisfied with all the crabmeat-filled dishes (plus, no crab surgery required!). \n\nService was truly friendly. The dogs are super local, nothing fancy (which was what we were going for) and certainly more clean and tidy than many of the other dingy seafood joints on the same street.\n\nCan't wait to come back here!\nRead more\nWritten June 24, 2018",
